            <ArticleTitle>First Whole-Genome Shotgun Sequence of a Promising Cellulase Secretor, Trichoderma koningiopsis Strain POS7.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e00823-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.00823-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Trichoderma koningiopsis strain POS7 produces significantly large amounts of cellulase enzymes in solid-state fermentation. The Illumina-based sequence analysis reveals an approximate genome size of 36.6 Mbp, with a G+C content of 48.82% for T. koningiopsis POS7. Based on ab initio prediction, 12,661 coding genes were annotated.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 Castrillo et al.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
